  "notation": "Env-Wt 607.04",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt600.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 607.04 Other Application Requirements",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 607.04 Other Application Requirements.\n\n(a) Prior to finalizing a dredge proposal, the applicant shall conduct an existing conditions bathymetric survey and submit it with the application to the department.\n\n(b) Prior to finalizing a dredge proposal, the applicant shall submit information regarding the current and historic presence of submerged aquatic vegetation, as documented by the CFA in Env-Wt 603.04, within and adjacent to the proposed dredging footprint.\n\n(c) As specified in RSA 482-A:3, X(b), the application fee for dredging in tidal waters/wetlands for the purpose of improving navigation for a municipality, as sponsored by DP&H, shall not exceed $10,000.\n\n(d) The application fee for all projects not covered by (c), above, shall be as specified in RSA 482-A:3, I(a)(3).\n\nSource. #12806, eff 12-15-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt600.html"
